      "slideNumber": 3,
      "title": "IN THE END OF THIS LESSON, WE WILL LEARN:",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "1.The article of SI and SINA 2.The article of ANG and MGA 3. Sentence formation",
          "isBullet": false
        }
      ],
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "slideNumber": 4,
      "title": "The Article SI and SINA The article SI is use before the name of a person and the plural article SINA is used before the name of two or more persons. Ex. Liza is a woman Si Liza ay babae Simon and Tom are good. Sina Simon at Tom ay mababait Helen and tom are children. Sina Helen at tom ay mga bata.",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Note that tagalog sentences follow a plurality rule where either the subject or predicate may be plural. However, the pluralization of both subject  and predicate is optional. In the sentence above, the article sina indicates that the subject is plural while mga ( a plural marker that has no meaning on its own) before bata indicates that the noun is plural.",
          "isBullet": false
        },
        {
          "text": "Adjective form their plural by duplicating the first syllable of the root word .",
          "isBullet": false
        },
        {
          "text": "For ex. (kind root word is bait) ma bait=singular of good\t\tprefix mababait ma ganda",
          "isBullet": false
        }
      ],
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "slideNumber": 5,
      "title": "The Article of ANG and MGA The article ANG is used before the name of a single thing or place while ANG MGA (manga) is used before the names of two or more things or places. Halimbawa : The child is good.\t\t\t\tAng bata ay mabait The children and the dogs are good. Ang mga bata at ang mga aso ay mababait .",
      "paragraphs": [],
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "slideNumber": 6,
      "title": "The article ANG",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The article ANG must always precede the name of a place . However, the article MANGA may be place before the adjective, which must then take on a plural form if there is more than one name of place in the subject , or before the noun. Ex.",
          "isBullet": false
        },
        {
          "text": "Ang Manila ay isang lungsod ng Pilipinas.\t\t\tManila is a city in the Philippines",
          "isBullet": false
        },
        {
          "text": "Ang Manila at ang Washington D.C ay mga lungsod Manila and Washington D.C are cities Note that it is acceptable to delete the second ANG before the second name of a place and the meaning of the sentence will not change",
          "isBullet": false
        }
      ],
      "images": []
    },
